  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Accommodation Facilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will ensure that unaccompanied migrant children (UMC) identified in precarious living conditions have improved access to immediate accommodation and assistance tailored to their best interest. This will be achieved through a two-fold approach, addressing both the affected population&#x2019;s needs as well as institutional gaps. Specifically, the project foresees the operation of emergency accommodation facilities (EAFs) where UMC will be hosted upon their identification and referral by the relevant authorities, namely SSPUAM, and until their placement to other care arrangements that are deemed suitable based on their best interest. On the institutional side, the SSPUAM&#x2019; s capacity in linking the EAFs with long-term solutions will be enhanced through the provision of technical support and specialized staff.</narrative>
  </description>
